2. In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires —
“aerosol‑generating feature”, in relation to a licensable aquatic facility, means a part or component of the licensable aquatic facility that is capable of producing a suspension of fine liquid droplets in air or other type of gas;
“aquatic facility licensee” means a person that holds a valid aquatic facility licence;
“multi‑use spa pool” has the meaning given by paragraph 2 of the Environmental Public Health (Licensable Aquatic Facilities) Order 2021 (G.N. No. S 643/2021);
“swimming pool” has the meaning given by paragraph 2 of the Environmental Public Health (Licensable Aquatic Facilities) Order 2021;
“water playground” has the meaning given by paragraph 2 of the Environmental Public Health (Licensable Aquatic Facilities) Order 2021.
